      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T21:04:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We provide a library secretkeeper_comm (aosp/2792898) which constructs requests/response/packet from the CBOR encoding specified in this spec \u0026 vice-versa.\n  \nThe Secretkeeper client (as well as VTS) uses this library. We will have serializaration/deserialtion VTS for each possible requests/response/error structures - aosp/2797757.\n\n\u003e How do we make sure the format used by the framework\n\nI\u0027m not sure I fully understand the question. As long as secretkeeper_comm library used is the same (or versioned in parallel to HAL versioning), we can enforce framework won\u0027t drift away from this definition.\n\nI cannot think of any stricter way to guard it. Ideas?",
      "parentUuid": "e81caa8a_af63d3b5",
      "revId": "5f7b9d0d5deea35f683168ed2f250d3a402bb469",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
